Found 2026-08-30 by codex reviewing B039, proven by experiment by the B039
lane, and confirmed independently by the coordinator by reading the code.
Out of B039's scope; filed separately, nothing touched.

## Defect

`src/config.rs:1538`:

    let auto_detected = config.openplanet_dir.clone();
    config.recheck_variant_folder(auto_detected.as_deref());

and inside `recheck_variant_folder` (`src/config.rs:1897`):

    // Replace the auto-detected dir only when it was the Layer-1 default
    // (not an explicit user override).
    if self.openplanet_dir.as_deref() == auto_detected {
        self.openplanet_dir = Some(p);
    }

`auto_detected` is a CLONE of `config.openplanet_dir` taken immediately
before the call, and nothing mutates `openplanet_dir` in between. **The guard
compares the value against a copy of itself, so it is always true.**

The clone is taken AFTER every config layer has applied, so by the time
`recheck_variant_folder` runs the code can no longer tell an explicitly
configured `openplanet_dir` from one Layer 1 auto-detected. The docstring two
lines up states the intent it cannot implement: "Only an explicit
`openplanet_dir` (config / init options) wins over the variant probe."

## Impact (user-facing)

A user who sets `openplanet_dir` explicitly AND a `game_target` whose variant
folder differs has their explicit setting **silently replaced** by
`$HOME/<variant>`. No warning. Their configured install is ignored in favour
of one the tool found on its own.

Demonstrated by the B039 lane: a synthetic HOME with
`~/.config/openplanet-lsp/config.toml` setting `game_target = "MP4"` and a
populated `$HOME/OpenplanetMP4` caused a test whose fixture pinned an EMPTY
`openplanet_dir` to load the fake install and report
`{"ok":true,"regenerated":4276}` — through a pin that was supposed to make
that impossible.

## Work

Capture whether `openplanet_dir` was set EXPLICITLY, and pass that, rather than
re-deriving it from a value that has already been through the ladder. The
provenance is knowable at the point each layer applies; it is only unknowable
at line 1538 because it was never recorded.

Note B050 already installs defines together with their ORIGINS
(`set_base_defines`) so introspection can report where a value came from. The
same shape of answer is what this needs. Check whether that origin tracking can
be extended rather than adding a parallel mechanism.

Do NOT fix by moving the clone earlier without recording provenance — an
earlier clone still cannot distinguish "explicitly set to the Layer-1 default"
from "auto-detected", and those must behave differently for the docstring to
be true.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)

Red: explicit `openplanet_dir = X` plus `game_target` naming a different
variant whose folder EXISTS under $HOME -> `openplanet_dir` must stay X.

Variants (per CLAUDE.md, generalize):
- explicit dir + matching target -> unchanged (already passes; pin it)
- explicit dir + non-matching target, variant folder EXISTS -> stays explicit
- explicit dir + non-matching target, variant folder ABSENT -> stays explicit
- NO explicit dir + non-matching target, folder exists -> IS re-probed (this
  is the behaviour GH #45 wanted and it must not regress)
- explicit dir set via init options rather than config.toml -> same protection
- explicit dir that happens to EQUAL the Layer-1 default, non-matching target
  -> stays put. This is the case that proves provenance is tracked rather
  than inferred from the value, and no value-comparison fix can pass it.
- a no-build target (MP3 / NATIONS_FOREVER) -> unchanged behaviour

Hermeticity: these tests probe $HOME by construction. Pin a synthetic HOME;
`just test-hermetic` must stay green.

## Related

GH #45 (introduced the variant re-probe), B039 (whose fixture this defeated —
that fixture now pins `game_target` as a workaround, which this ticket should
make unnecessary), B050 (define origins — precedent for provenance tracking).